  "reason": "RNA-only evidence is strongest for multiprofile scvi_n200, with avgpool reaching 0.6501 accuracy and transformer 0.6530, while image-only models are weak around 0.33. The main remaining uncertainty is whether adding image information to the strong scvi RNA representation improves performance. config_036 tests this by extending the tested scvi_n200 multiprofile avgpool RNA baseline with imagenet_vit_l image features using the same avgpool aggregation and a simple concat fusion. This is the best next experiment because it directly probes the highest-value untested choice—multimodal fusion—while minimizing confounds from untested transformer image aggregation or weighted fusion."
